Figure 1: (a) Query–Skill Misalignment. Task queries and
skills are naturally formulated from different perspectives,
with queries specifying desired objectives and skills describe
execution guidelines. In the example, rich legal-domain se-
mantics make skills for legal analysis appear highly relevant,
while those actually required for task execution is ranked
much lower. (b) Statistics. The statistics further verify this
