Details of the Datasets
We evaluate the proposed method SkillDreamer on two skill-
retrieval datasets, including SkillRet (Cho, Kang, and Kim
2026) and SkillUsage (Liu et al. 2026).
• SkillRet is a large-scale benchmark constructed from pub-
lic skills collected from open-source communities. It gen-
erates natural language queries from sampled skills using
an LLM, with the sampled skills serving as the corre-
sponding retrieval targets.
• SkillUsage is a benchmark built upon SkillsBench (Li
et al. 2026). It contains executable tasks and their cor-
responding skills, which are integrated into a large-scale
library of real-world skills for skill retrieval evaluation.
