Details of the Prompts
We present the prompts employed in the CI and PSG mod-
ules of SkillDreamer, respectively. Specifically, the prompt
for the CI module guides the LLM to identify self-contained,
retrieval-oriented capability requirements while preserving
essential evidence from the original query, as shown in Ta-
ble 5. Based on these inferred requirements and their pre-
served evidence, the prompt for the PSG module further gen-
erates concise hypothetical SKILL.md documents enriched
with solution-oriented knowledge. The complete prompt is
provided in Table 6.
Details of the Baselines
We consider three categories of retrieval baselines in our
experiments. The details of the corresponding baseline re-
trievers are provided as follows:
• Sparse Retrieval. BM25 (Robertson and Zaragoza 2009)
is adopted as the representative sparse retriever, ranking
skills through term-level matching between the query and
skill documents.
• General
Embedding
Retrieval.
Qwen3-
Embedding (Zhang et al. 2025) performs instruction-
aware dense semantic matching, while BGE-large-
