RetroMAE


Role. You are an expert in decomposing tasks into capability requirements for skill retrieval.
Raw Task. {query}
Goal. Identify the independent capabilities required to complete the raw task and write one retrieval-oriented subquery for each
capability. These subqueries will later be used to generate hypothetical pseudo-skills.
Decomposition Principles.
• Decompose the task by independent capability requirements, rather than execution steps.
• Preserve relevant technical domains, methods, tools, and constraints from the raw task.
• Specialized artifact processing may be treated as an independent capability when it requires specific technical expertise.
• Do not invent capabilities, tools, methods, or requirements unsupported by the raw task.
Output Requirements.
Return JSON only. Generate one to five subqueries. Each subquery should contain a capability name, a concise and
self-contained retrieval requirement, and exact supporting evidence copied from the raw task.
Output Format.
{
“is_multi_intent”: true,
“num_subqueries”: 2,
“split_reason”: “Basis for the capability division.”,
“subqueries”: [
{
“id”: “q1”,
“retrieval_intent”: “Capability name”,
“subquery”: “Self-contained capability requirement.”,
“preserved_query_evidence”: [
“Exact phrase copied from the raw task.”
]
}
]
}
Table 5: Prompt used for capability-aware query decomposition in the CI module.
Role. Write one concise, retrieval-oriented skill for a single capability.
Inputs. {subquery} and {preserved_evidence}
Goal. Generate one hypothetical SKILL.md that describes a reusable skill capable of handling the given capability
requirement. The skill should provide useful solution knowledge rather than simply restating the subquery.
Generation Principles.
• Teach how to perform the capability instead of repeating the original subquery.
• Incorporate concrete domain knowledge, such as methods, algorithms, APIs, workflows, failure handling, or validation.
• Preserve capability-defining technical terms and constraints.
• Do not invent unsupported facts or broaden the skill into adjacent capabilities.
• Produce a concise, reusable, and standalone skill using only capability-specific sections.
Output Requirements.
Return only the complete SKILL.md content. The generated skill must follow the specified metadata structure and contain a
concise skill name, trigger-oriented description, and a human-readable title.
Output Format.
--
name: short-lowercase-kebab-case-name
description: “Concise, trigger-oriented description of the capability.”
--
# Human-Readable Skill Title
Write the task-adaptive skill body.
Table 6: Prompt used for pseudo-skill generation in the PSG module.


